1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,800
IN ONE INSTANT, THE GROUND CRUMBLES.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,670
HERE'S WHY.

3
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:10,570
8 — Atomic number · oxygen
Third most common element in the universe.

4
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:13,010
21% — Of the air (by volume)

5
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:15,310
~65% — Of your body's mass

6
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:17,750
46% — Of earth's crust, by mass

7
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:22,020
IMPOSSIBLE — Matter can't just vanish
We did hydrogen. Let's ruin oxygen too.

8
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:24,720
DELETE IT.

9
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,020
T = 0
Every oxygen atom. Everywhere. At once.

10
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:33,550
0.77 atm — Air pressure at sea level
The air just lost 23% of its weight.

11
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:39,140
~2,200 m — It feels like this altitude
Your ears pop. Enjoy it. It's the last thing you'll notice.

12
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:44,950
−45 kg — From a 70 kg person
Hydrogen took 7 kg. Oxygen takes 45. New record.

13
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:49,960
H₂O → H₂ — Your water becomes hydrogen gas
About 7 kg of it, packed into a body.

14
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:54,630
>1,000 atm — Rough lower bound
Denser than liquid hydrogen. It does not stay inside.

15
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,530
POP. AGAIN.

16
00:00:56,530 --> 00:01:01,490
0 — Fires · explosions · engines
Fire needs oxygen. Nothing can burn now. Not even you.

17
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:07,020
46% — Of the crust is oxygen
Rock is mostly oxides. Sand, clay, granite: oxygen.

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:09,420
THE GROUND CRUMBLES.

19
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:13,860
53% — Of glass (silica) is oxygen
Windows: optional. Concrete and brick: also oxides.

20
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:17,900
STEEL — Survives
Iron has almost no oxygen. Congratulations to steel.

21
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:23,030
1.57 × 10²⁰ kg — Of hydrogen left from the oceans
Water minus oxygen is just hydrogen.

22
00:01:23,030 --> 00:01:28,040
≈30× — The mass of today's air
If it all stayed as a gas around Earth.

23
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:33,340
THE MOST FLAMMABLE SKY EVER.
And not one thing left to light it with.

24
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:38,530
97–99% — Of the sun's medium uv · blocked by ozone
Ozone is three oxygen atoms.

25
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:43,030
0% — Blocked now
UV protection: cancelled. Luckily, nothing is left to sunburn.

26
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:48,270
~30% — Of earth's mass is oxygen
Earth loses about 1.8 × 10²⁴ kg.

27
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:53,230
24 Moons — Of mass · gone
Earth is still here. Just a lot less of it.

28
00:01:53,230 --> 00:01:57,670
0.57% — Of the sun is oxygen
The Sun barely notices. It keeps shining.

29
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:01,260
EARTH STAYS IN ORBIT.
Unlike last time.

30
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:07,250
MARS — Red because of iron oxide (rust)
Delete oxygen and the Red Planet stops being red.

31
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:11,810
EUROPA · ENCELADUS — Moons with hidden oceans
Our best bets for alien life. Water worlds.

32
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:15,110
WERE.
Every water ocean in existence: gone.

33
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:21,110
H vs O — Pick your apocalypse
Hydrogen: Earth flies away. Oxygen: Earth stays, and crumbles.

34
00:02:21,110 --> 00:02:24,120
WHICH ELEMENT SHOULD WE DELETE NEXT?

35
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:28,720
COMMENT. BEFORE WE RUN OUT.
Thought experiment. Not physically possible.

